33,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Minako,,The fixed costs are higher than some of us might have assumed. We need to decide if these are split equally or by usage.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems the friction isn't just about the money, but the psychological weight of ""asking for favors"" and the clash of routine.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The handover state is unacceptable. We are treating the car as a shared resource, but some are treating it as a rental they don't have to clean.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The fuel receipts are quite revealing. Some of us have been far more generous than others, while some have been practically invisible.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,I... I found out that just recording the runs takes a lot of time. Almost an hour a week just to be accurate.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, if fuel is the main point of contention, we can separate fuel costs from the fixed maintenance costs.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, while cleanliness is a virtue, I suspect the ""clipped replies"" we've noticed stem from the routine clashes I've discovered.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, a ""routine clash"" is a luxury. Not being able to leave for work because the car is dirty or empty is a failure of the system.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Minako, separating them is logical. But we must first acknowledge the debt owed by those who haven't contributed to the fuel.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I just... I worry that if we make the rules too strict, we'll spend even more time arguing about the records.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minako,,"We must avoid emotional arguments. The fact is that a ""share is a share"" only works if the usage is equal. It isn't.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely. If we simply move the ""sore point"" to a stricter ledger, we will still be unhappy. We need a system that reduces the need to ask favors.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,A system that reduces favors is one where the car is always ready for the next person. That requires a mandatory handover checklist.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"A checklist is a tool, not a solution. The solution is a financial correction. We need a monthly flat fee plus a fuel-usage surcharge.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,Um... maybe we could just... simplify it? So we don't have to spend so many evenings sorting it out?,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minako,,"I agree with Shion on the structure, but we must ensure the flat fee covers the tax and insurance fairly.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I can support a flat fee if it removes the need for constant negotiation. Let's ensure the ""routine"" trips are pre-allocated.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I will only agree to a financial plan if it includes a strict penalty for returning the car in a poor state.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Penalties are tedious to enforce. Let's stick to the numbers. A flat fee for fixed costs, and a usage-based payment for fuel.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think I can agree to that, as long as it doesn't make the paperwork even harder.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
