60,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Option B is the most equitable. It accounts for the actual usage hours and fuel, ensuring no one is quietly subsidizing another.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option A is far more elegant. It eliminates the ""favor"" dynamic and the constant negotiation of a calendar. It provides stability.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option A is the only one that solves the midweek morning problem. If I know the car is mine on Tuesday, I know it's there.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,"Option B is the only one that provides the ""honest picture"" I want. A flat fee is too easy for the heavy users to exploit.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think Option A sounds better. It means we don't have to... you know... arrange things every single evening.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, @Asuka, @Daisuke, while Option A is simpler, it ignores the reality that some of us use the car significantly more than others.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Asuka"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, the ""inequity"" of a few extra miles is a small price to pay for the restoration of our social harmony.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Minako, the ""inequity"" of a calendar is the stress of not knowing if the car is available when you have a deadline.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, harmony is a facade if the financial burden is uneven. Option B is the only logical choice for a joint investment.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I just... I really don't want to spend more time... untangling who owes what. Option B sounds like more work.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minako,,"If we choose Option A, we must adjust the monthly fee based on the ""value"" of the days. Weekends are more valuable than Tuesdays.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Now we are returning to the very complexity I wish to avoid. Let us keep it simple: equal days, equal pay.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I can accept equal pay for equal days. The predictability of the car's presence is my primary requirement.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, your ""simplicity"" is just a way to avoid the numbers. I cannot support a system that allows guesswork to continue.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think I'm with Benjamin and Asuka. I just want it to be... quiet.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minako,,"I see the majority prefers simplicity over precision. While I believe B is fairer, I will not be the only one fighting for it.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"A wise concession, Minako. Logic dictates that the most sustainable system is the one the group can actually tolerate.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I'm voting for A. It's the only way to ensure the car is ready when I need it.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shion,,"I will vote for B. I prefer a system based on reality rather than a convenient fiction of ""equal use.""","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'm voting for A too. Please.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
